per is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-lcm-gap-engine"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-lcm-gap-engine"],"id":"long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.17 (Irrationality from a gap beyond the preceding least common multiple)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.17, p. 49, label thm:lcm-gap-engine","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For an integer base $b\\ge2$ and strictly increasing support $a:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N$ with $a(0)\\ge\n1$: if $a(k)-\\mathrm{lcm}(a(0),\\dots,a(k-1))\\to\\infty$, then $\\sum'_k 1/(b^{a(k)}-1)$ is irrational. The base may vary over the integers, but the denominators remain $b^{a(k)}-1$. Applying the argument to another denominator sequence would require its own divisibility and tail estimates.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-lcm-gap-engine%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_of_lcm_gap%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-lcm-gap-engine%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_of_lcm_gap%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_of_lcm_gap"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-lcm-gap-engine","id":"field:0d4166ca3aa4540ca86e9680992919f03d563ca18f43390cfd2c1eb396d9b87e","kind":"evidence_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4